Package: RobustMediate
Title: Causal Mediation Analysis with Diagnostics and Sensitivity
        Analysis
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Subir", "Hait", email = "haitsubi@msu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-9871-9677"))
Description: Provides tools for causal mediation analysis with continuous
    treatments. Estimates natural direct and indirect effects by g-computation
    over a user-defined treatment grid, with bootstrap intervals that can
    resample whole clusters, and supports nonlinear dose-response through
    spline terms in the model formulas. Includes balance diagnostics based on
    standardized mean differences and stabilized inverse probability
    weights. Provides sensitivity analysis for
    confounding of the mediator-outcome relationship using the error
    correlation parameter of Imai, Keele, and Yamamoto (2010)
    <doi:10.1214/10-STS321>, and path-wise and indirect-effect robustness
    values in the partial R-squared metric of Cinelli and Hazlett (2020)
    <doi:10.1111/rssb.12348>, for both joint-significance and Sobel tests of
    the indirect effect. Additional utilities include visualization of
    dose-response mediation functions and formatted outputs for applied
    research.
